  mensaje1: 'Growing Food in Space: Astronauts can grow leafy vegetables like lettuce aboard the International Space Station! Potatoes are also being studied because they are rich in calories and could help astronauts grow food on the Moon and Mars.'
  mensaje2: Can Plants Grow on Mars? Not directly in Martian soil! Mars' natural soil, called regolith, contains toxic salts. Plants would need special growing beds with clean, treated soil inside a space base.
